        <mxCell id="8mh4Gha9_1KVUytQgeUW-273" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="Weak pointer &lt;font face=&quot;Lucida Console&quot;&gt;wp_person&lt;/font&gt; solves this problem. The &lt;font face=&quot;Lucida Console&quot;&gt;Car&lt;/font&gt; just needs to &lt;i&gt;observe&lt;/i&gt; the &lt;font face=&quot;Lucida Console&quot;&gt;Person&lt;/font&gt; and not really have some ownership of it. Since&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: &amp;quot;Lucida Console&amp;quot;;&quot;&gt;wp_person&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;i&gt;does not contribute to &lt;font face=&quot;Lucida Console&quot;&gt;RC&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/i&gt;, as soon as &lt;font face=&quot;Lucida Console&quot;&gt;sp_person_1&lt;/font&gt; is destroyed the &lt;b&gt;Person&lt;/b&gt; object memory will be freed. This destroys &lt;font face=&quot;Lucida Console&quot;&gt;sp_car&lt;/font&gt; freeing &lt;font face=&quot;Lucida Console&quot;&gt;Car&lt;/font&gt; object memory." vertex="1">
